{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' review-room/surprise-v1_critique/captions.srt\"","aggregated_output":"1\n00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,210\nAn ordinary afternoon at Kneaded A.I.\n\n2\n00:00:05,299 --> 00:00:07,157\nThe team can't agree on the opening line.\n\n3\n00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:14,359\nStop wasting opens on the pain, not the promise. First impressions should inspire, not scold.\n\n4\n00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,710\nSomeone presents the fix.\n\n5\n00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,345\nThey take it to the boss. Who has notes. A lot of notes.\n\n6\n00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:24,481\nExcept, there is no team.\n\n7\n00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,048\nEvery session is an agent. One connector runs them all.\n\n8\n00:00:34,299 --> 00:00:35,481\nThe debate was a group chat.\n\n9\n00:00:38,299 --> 00:00:39,626\nThe presenter was A.I.\n\n10\n00:00:42,299 --> 00:00:43,432\nAnd so was the boss.\n\n11\n00:00:45,299 --> 00:00:46,939\nThis is how Kneaded A.I. works.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"The twist is understandable, but it does not fully “land” because the AI reveal leaks too early. By 12s and 18s, we already see “AGENT,” “Group Chat,” “Claude,” and a generated deck, so the audience is ahead of the film before “Except, there is no team.” The emotional arc is solid: ordinary office, debate, fix, boss pressure, reveal, replay. The main issue is withholding. First act should feel more human and mundane; second act should make the same beats snap into AI logic.\n\nPacing is clear but slightly explanatory. The replay works, though the boss reveal needs a stronger visual payoff.\n\nTop 3 frame changes:\n- 12s: Remove “AGENT 1/2,” “Claude,” and “Group Chat” from the first pass. Show a human meeting beat or a generic chat without AI labels; save the agent UI for the replay.\n- 18s: “Tell Claude what you want” gives away the premise. Replace with a normal-looking presentation slide in the first pass, then reveal the Claude/deck interface at 39s.\n- 42s: “And so was the boss” currently looks like a normal executive scene. Add an unmistakable AI boss overlay: comment stack, review agent name, automated notes, or the boss shot dissolving into an agent card.\n\nCodex"}}
